[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906640280","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-2906640280","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":2906640280,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tP8-Y","user":{"login":"allhailcheese","id":37654973,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM3NjU0OTcz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/37654973?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese","html_url":"https://github.com/allhailcheese","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/allhailcheese/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T08:43:04Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T08:43:04Z","body":" Calling `Resize` directly with the new size will cause `O(n)` behavior when repeatedly `AddRange`ing a singular item. More generally, it will harm the use case of `AddRange`ing a small list.\r\n\r\nThe .NET implementation uses `Grow`, an internal function implemented [here](https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/87b35f477c09f146107a6c11627317f6b15e9d3e/src/libraries/System.Private.CoreLib/src/System/Collections/Generic/List.cs#L451), which calls `GetNewCapacity`, which returns the max between the given new size and the current size times 2. This makes sure repeated uses of `AddRange` with a small list does not degrade performance relative to repeated `Add`.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906640280/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906644920","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-2906644920","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":2906644920,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6tP-G4","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-05-24T08:53:07Z","updated_at":"2025-05-24T08:53:07Z","body":"@eyalzus12 \r\n\r\n> The .NET implementation uses Grow\r\n\r\nYou are correct, and I'm aware of that; however, what I did is merely mirror the identical logic implemented in the original `AddRange(IEtor)`, I can implement the DOTNET-BCL-styled resizing logic if the team is okay with changing this behavior for performance.\r\n\r\n[Link](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/6fd4b7a775f3c70805dc42d78535710d971877c5/modules/mono/glue/GodotSharp/GodotSharp/Core/Array.cs#L1661)\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\npublic void AddRange(IEnumerable<T> collection)\r\n{\r\n    ThrowIfReadOnly();\r\n\r\n    if (collection == null)\r\n        throw new ArgumentNullException(nameof(collection), \"Value cannot be null.\");\r\n\r\n    // If the collection is another Godot Array, we can add the items\r\n    // with a single interop call.\r\n    if (collection is Array array)\r\n    {\r\n        var self = (godot_array)_underlyingArray.NativeValue;\r\n        var collectionNative = (godot_array)array.NativeValue;\r\n        _ = NativeFuncs.godotsharp_array_add_range(ref self, collectionNative);\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n    if (collection is Array<T> typedArray)\r\n    {\r\n        var self = (godot_array)_underlyingArray.NativeValue;\r\n        var collectionNative = (godot_array)typedArray._underlyingArray.NativeValue;\r\n        _ = NativeFuncs.godotsharp_array_add_range(ref self, collectionNative);\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    // If we can retrieve the count of the collection without enumerating it\r\n    // (e.g.: the collections is a List<T>), use it to resize the array once\r\n    // instead of growing it as we add items.\r\n    if (collection.TryGetNonEnumeratedCount(out int count))\r\n    {\r\n        int oldCount = Count;\r\n        Resize(Count + count);\r\n\r\n        using var enumerator = collection.GetEnumerator();\r\n\r\n        for (int i = 0; i < count; i++)\r\n        {\r\n            enumerator.MoveNext();\r\n            this[oldCount + i] = enumerator.Current;\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        return;\r\n    }\r\n\r\n    foreach (var item in collection)\r\n    {\r\n        Add(item);\r\n    }\r\n}\r\n```","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2906644920/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078264384","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-4078264384","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":4078264384,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zFWBA","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-17T22:05:37Z","updated_at":"2026-03-17T22:05:37Z","body":"Matching the logic of the existing overloads is the correct thing to do. The `AddRange(IEnumerable)` overload was implemented using `resize` because, as far as I remember, the Godot array didn't expose the capacity at the time. I think this changed with https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105928 which now exposes a `reserve` method we could use instead.\r\n\r\nI think it could make sense to use `reserve` instead of `resize`, provided that the `reserve` method is **exposed** (which it [doesn't seem to be](https://github.com/godotengine/godot/blob/29d2c7ece514127cc449ce37994ef4b369a3a9c6/core/variant/variant_call.cpp#L2676-L2728)). If we wanted to make this change, we should discuss exposing `reserve` first, but I think it's out of scope for this PR anyway.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4078264384/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080682098","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-4080682098","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":4080682098,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zOkRy","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-18T08:36:29Z","updated_at":"2026-03-18T08:36:29Z","body":"> If we wanted to make this change, we should discuss exposing reserve first, but I think it's out of scope for this PR anyway.\r\n\r\nI think we can keep this PR so there is at least an available API surface for developers, and improve performance once the `reserve` is available later.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4080682098/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087875263","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-4087875263","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":4087875263,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zqAa_","user":{"login":"raulsntos","id":3903059,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjM5MDMwNTk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3903059?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos","html_url":"https://github.com/raulsntos","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/raulsntos/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T05:16:55Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T05:16:55Z","body":"Sounds good to me. We'll also have to add an overload with `T[]` to avoid ambiguity in cases like this:\r\n\r\n```csharp\r\ngodotArray.AddRange(new int[] { 1, 2, 3 });\r\n```\r\n\r\nAlthough, if we move to .NET 10, we can use the `[OverloadResolutionPriority]` attribute which I think would be better.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4087875263/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4088177416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-4088177416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":4088177416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7zrKMI","user":{"login":"Delsin-Yu","id":71481700,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcxNDgxNzAw","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/71481700?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu","html_url":"https://github.com/Delsin-Yu","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Delsin-Yu/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-03-19T06:50:06Z","updated_at":"2026-03-19T06:50:06Z","body":"Added. A second thought: the AddRange method could also greatly benefit from the `reserve` method, since our manual resizing of the array to the exact length might not be optimal.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4088177416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173510289","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106765#issuecomment-4173510289","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/106765","id":4173510289,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc74wraR","user":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-04-01T23:14:51Z","updated_at":"2026-04-01T23:14:51Z","body":"Thanks!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/4173510289/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]